From 030f50c9d6bb4a212269bf23acd1ba4b219c7d90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gavin_darkglider <rbrown4014@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:58:37 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] core: switch to verbose mode with Vol- too, and watch every
 key device

Devices without a keyboard (handhelds, tablets, the Nintendo Switch)
have no F2; Vol- now does what F2 does.  The volume keys are usually a
device of their own (gpio-keys, "ThinkPad Extra Buttons"), apart from a
keyboard that may also be plugged in, so:

- fbsplash_set_evdev() finds every input device whose key capabilities
  include F2 or Vol- (from sysfs) and sends them all, separated by
  commas; the old guesses stay as the fallback.
- 'set event dev' takes such a list; the daemon polls up to 8 devices.
- The default boot messages say "Press F2 or Vol- for verbose mode."

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
